{"i":521,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Bex","text":"Ash has called R every safe row so far, but I don't trust him. Last row R was weak; maybe this row is L to avoid pattern, but no pattern exists. I'll counter L to protect myself and shift blame if wrong."}
{"i":523,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Cole","text":"Ash called R for Bex on row 8 and has a pact with Eli (dead). Ash's calls have killed walkers; Hana's last words accuse Ash. Revealed weak panes on rows 1,2,4,5,6,7 were all R, so L may be safe, but past rows are independent; Ash's call of R is suspect. Counter L leaves me unaffe"}
{"i":524,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Dara","text":"Ash is the guide and called R. Bex is front and will step. I need to survive to final three. If I counter, Bex might listen and survive or die. If Bex dies, I become front. Ash has killed with calls before (Gus, and indirectly Fenn/Hana via counters). But Hana's last words blame "}
{"i":532,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Bex","text":"I counter-called L, and Cole also called L. But Ash called R. I have no proof. The weak panes don't follow a pattern. I trust my own read? I must decide; if wrong I fall, but at least Cole might go next. I'll step L to match my counter-call."}
